28-4:
Was getting into issues when training where the loss would become non-finite (NaN or Inf), which would cause the training to break. To address this, I implemented a few changes:
1. Add batch-level debug logging
2. Save non-finite batch tensors to disk
3. Run training to capture debug files
4. Inspect saved debug files to identify the source of non-finite values
5. Checkpoint saving didn't work due to non-finite values, so I added a check to skip saving checkpoints when non-finite values are detected in the loss or model parameters. This way, I can prevent the training process from breaking and focus on debugging the issue.

Two fixes for more non-finite values:

In loss/yolov1_loss.py, IoU target for confidence is now detached
max_iou_val = max_iou_val.detach(). This prevents unstable gradients flowing through circle IoU math (acos branch can be numerically nasty).
In tools/train.py, optimizer steps are now guarded
Added gradients_are_finite(...)
If gradients are non-finite, it skips optimizer.step() and logs it instead of poisoning weights.
Also removed the unconditional end-of-epoch optimizer step; now remainder-step only happens when accumulation leaves leftovers.
