Implement training curves to plot train/val loss and mAP over epochs for both models.
Here's a summary of what was added and how to use it:

What changed

File	Change
Yolov1-PyTorch/tools/train.py	import json, import math; circles key in collate_function; _circle_iou_scalar + _run_circle_val_map helper functions; JSON log init/resume + per-epoch mAP eval + log save in train()
Yolov1-PyTorch/config/voc.yaml	Added eval_map_interval: 1 and log_fname: 'training_log_circle.json'
Yolov1-PyTorch Baseline/tools/train.py	import json; _get_iou + _run_box_val_map helpers; same JSON logging pattern
Yolov1-PyTorch Baseline/config/voc.yaml	Added eval_map_interval: 1 and log_fname: 'training_log_baseline.json'
Thesis/plot_curves.py	New plotting script
Workflow

Train circle model: python -m tools.train --config config/voc.yaml

→ writes C:/temp/broccoli_training/training_log_circle.json

Train baseline model (from the Baseline dir): python -m tools.train --config config/voc.yaml

→ writes C:/temp/broccoli_training/training_log_baseline.json

Plot at any time (even mid-training): python plot_curves.py

→ saves C:/temp/broccoli_training/training_curves.png

Key notes

eval_map_interval: 1 means mAP is computed every epoch. Set to 5 to speed up training if it's too slow.
The log is resumed automatically if training is restarted from a checkpoint.
Both log files coexist in the same C:/temp/broccoli_training directory. Note that both models also share the same checkpoint names (yolo_broccoli.pth), so you should train them sequentially rather than simultaneously to avoid overwriting each other's checkpoints.

